icon-scan-resume-through-non-resumable-while-condition
jtran is the full 17-module translator and does not build in either mode: the compiler
itself aborts. m3: `bb_emit_end: 2 unresolved forward reference(s)`; m4 emits an .s that
assembles but fails at ld with `undefined reference to n<N>_var_β`. Both sites are in
lexer.icn's `yylex`/`lex_yylex0`, on the shape `EXPR ? { while COND do ... suspend ... }`.
Root-caused 2026-09-03 (hq_B), minimal witness (2 lines, in the FINDING): the scan's
resume operand is the while's loop-back GOTO, whose beta-follow lands on the loop
CONDITION's beta port -- and a non-resumable condition (a literal or a plain variable)
emits only an alpha entry. `while f()` (resumable condition) compiles and links fine.
Routed to hq_C: the fix needs a resume-at-alpha marker, which the 2-ref IR_t
(FROZEN LABEL MODEL, GOAL-JCON-IN-SCRIP.md) has no room for today.
